CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ prvalues bind to const T &: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
When a named function parameter pack was expanded for the instance, each
element replaced the whole decl-specifier of `const T &...t', dropping
its const: `count(i, 2)' instantiated `count(int &, int &)', which a
prvalue cannot bind to.
